{"content":[{"c":["AMRAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Kohath’s son, a member of Levi’s tribe. Amram married Jochebed and had three famous children: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.16-20","r":"Exod.6.16-20","rawR":"Exod.6.16-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.16-20","value":"Exod.6.16-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:16-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.58-59","r":"Num.26.58-59","rawR":"Num.26.58-59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.58-59","value":"Num.26.58-59"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:58-59"},"). During the Israelites’ wilderness journey, the responsibility of the Amramites was to care for the ark and the table, lampstand, altars, and other furnishings used in the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.27,31","r":"Num.3.27,31","rawR":"Num.3.27,31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.27,31","value":"Num.3.27,31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:27, 31"},"). Later, the Amramites were one of the groups in charge of offerings placed in the temple treasury (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.23-24","r":"1Chr.26.23-24","rawR":"1Chr.26.23-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.23-24","value":"1Chr.26.23-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:23-24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Priest from Bani’s family, who obeyed Ezra’s exhortation to divorce his pagan wife after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.34","r":"Ezra.10.34","rawR":"Ezra.10.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.34","value":"Ezra.10.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. KJV form of Hamran, Dishon’s son, in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.41","r":"1Chr.1.41","rawR":"1Chr.1.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.41","value":"1Chr.1.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 1:41"},". Hamran itself is an alternate form of Hemdan (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.26","r":"Gen.36.26","rawR":"Gen.36.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.26","value":"Gen.36.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:26"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Hemdan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Hemdan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Hemdan_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Hemdan"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Amram","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 6:16-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.6.16-20","rawQueryValue":"Exod.6.16-20","sourceRefExact":"Exod.6.16-20"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:58-59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.58-59","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.58-59","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.58-59"},{"anchorText":"Nm 3:27, 31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.3.27,31","rawQueryValue":"Num.3.27,31","sourceRefExact":"Num.3.27,31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:23-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.23-24","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.23-24","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.23-24"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.34","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.34","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.34"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 1:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.41"},{"anchorText":"Gn 36:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.36.26","rawQueryValue":"Gen.36.26","sourceRefExact":"Gen.36.26"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"efe2e18825adc57a50dc53bc5470deaef84fe291491027c8839035e00bc16889","sourceItemName":"Amram","sourceItemOrder":318,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Amram","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Amram","title":"Amram","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0